# Credential and secret locations, one glob per line, ~ = $HOME.
# This file REPLACES the `Read(...)` entries that used to live in
# permissions.deny. They had to go: any Read() deny rule arms two Claude Code
# checks on a compound command containing a `cd`, one of them immune to bypass
# mode, and those checks prompted on ordinary read-only commands (measured
# repeatedly on 2026-09-03/04). protect-credentials.sh enforces this list with
# a PreToolUse hook `deny`, which short-circuits every permission mode.
#
# Derived from the union of both config homes' former Read() rules. Keeping
# them in sync is the point: adding a line here is the only way to protect a
# new path now.
~/.ssh/**
~/.gnupg/**
~/.aws/**
~/.azure/**
~/.config/gh/**
~/.git-credentials
~/.docker/config.json
~/.kube/**
~/.npmrc
~/.npm/**
~/.pypirc
~/.gem/credentials
~/Library/Keychains/**
~/Library/Application Support/**/metamask*/**
~/Library/Application Support/**/electrum*/**
~/Library/Application Support/**/exodus*/**
~/Library/Application Support/**/phantom*/**
~/Library/Application Support/**/solflare*/**
~/.electrum/**
~/.config/Exodus/**
~/.config/BraveSoftware/**/Extensions/**
~/.config/google-chrome/**/Extensions/**
~/.config/chromium/**/Extensions/**
~/.mozilla/firefox/**
